Subject: [PATCH 2/5] src/lab-process-mail: Package it and install under
 ~/local
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: mrrotkposnylsqlszqsztrmyzpkowont

lab-process-mail only protects itself from edits when it runs from a
copy outside the tree. A FreeBSD package makes that copy the same way
every time, and pkg tracks what it installed, so an upgrade or removal
leaves nothing stale behind.

The package carries no LOCALBASE. Its files are bin/ and share/
relative to whatever root pkg installs into, so "just install" puts
them under ~/local the way a port lands under /usr/local, and the
script finds its prompt relative to its own location. The same
package can later move into a real port unchanged.
